`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:[e.jsx(n.strong,{children:"Adapter implication:"})," custom-drawn controls/gameplay need project-authored semantic mappings appropriate to the intended roles, descriptions, state/value and actions; default names/hierarchy are not automatic interpretation of pixels, collision, quest completion or spatial playability. The low-level 4.5 DisplayServer API supports this semantic authoring, including sub-elements; it does not supply an external scene-state oracle. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/doc/classes/DisplayServer.xml",children:"Pinned DisplayServer API"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["The 4.5 documented screen-reader capability covers Windows, macOS and Linux X11/Wayland. Verify the actual build's capability: Windows source conditions it on a live accessibility driver, and initialization failure clears that driver. Do not infer mobile/Web delivery from the engine's export list. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/classes/class_displayserver.html#class-displayserver-constant-feature-accessibility-screen-reader",children:"4.5 capability"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/platform/windows/display_server_windows.cpp#L157-L165",children:"Windows capability"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/platform/windows/display_server_windows.cpp#L6806-L6817",children:"driver initialization"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["Pinned ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"DisplayServerHeadless::has_feature()"})," always returns false. Combined with the initial capability check in ",e.jsx(n.code,{children:"SceneTree::is_accessibility_enabled()"})," and its flush guard, this gates off the normal SceneTree→native-driver update path even in Always Active. This does not rule out a synthetic/custom unit-test tree; such a test still would not prove native OS delivery or assistive usability. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/servers/display_server_headless.h#L68-L70",children:"Headless"}),", ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/876b290332ec6f2e6d173d08162a02aa7e6ca46d/scene/main/scene_tree.cpp#L205-L310",children:"enabled/flush gates"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"proposed-acceptance-fixture-explicitly-unimplemented-and-unexecuted",children:"Proposed acceptance fixture: explicitly unimplemented and unexecuted"}),`
`,e.jsx(n.p,{children:"Use a disposable project-owned screen with a toggle action, a custom-drawn status indicator backed by independently observable state, an accessibility-only focus target, and a popup. Freeze the expected semantic contract and action effect before execution."}),`
