`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"bevy--remote-protocol",children:"Bevy · Remote Protocol"}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["Exposes ECS inspection and mutation through a JSON-RPC interface embedded in a Bevy application. RemotePlugin installs protocol operations but does not start a transport; RemoteHttpPlugin adds HTTP communication. Queries depend on registered, reflectable types, and non-strict reads can include per-component errors. The source link pins the file reviewed, not an executed build. Network access and mutation permissions require an explicit application policy. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/blob/85503941e488152711a4695bbe248e9ed9f453fc/crates/bevy_remote/src/lib.rs",children:"Primary source"}),". ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/blob/85503941e488152711a4695bbe248e9ed9f453fc/examples/app/headless_renderer.rs",children:"Windowless renderer example at checked commit"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"houdini-engine--pdg-api",children:"Houdini Engine · PDG API"}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["Controls procedural task-graph cooking and retrieves work-item events, states, and output paths. HAPI supports asynchronous full cooking, polling, pause, and cancellation; generate-only mode is always blocking even when the blocking argument is zero. Cached success differs from newly executed work, and a new cook can discard uncollected events. Preserve scheduler paths and drain events before another cook. Cancellation must be followed by terminal-state inspection. Houdini licensing and host configuration remain deployment requirements. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/hengine/_h_a_p_i__p_d_g.html",children:"Primary source"}),". ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/hengine/group___p_d_g.html",children:"PDG function reference"}),". ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/hom/commandline",children:"Command-line Python and license lifecycle"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"o3de--editor-automation",children:"O3DE · Editor Automation"}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["Exposes editor functionality through Python bindings and external editor-test orchestration. The PythonEditorBindings gem exposes editor C++ functionality through EBus and requires project configuration and an editor rebuild. External pytest and LyTestTools can launch the editor while embedded scripts drive it. Preserve both external and editor logs. These interfaces do not establish runtime Python support or a graphics-free execution profile. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://www.docs.o3de.org/docs/user-guide/editor/editor-automation/",children:"Primary source"}),". ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://docs.o3de.org/docs/user-guide/testing/parallel-pattern/",children:"Parallel editor test patterns"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"maya--standalone-python-and-file-operations",children:"Maya · Standalone Python and File Operations"}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["Initializes Maya outside an interactive session for scripted scene processing. Standalone initialization provides Maya libraries to Python scripts; file commands handle opening, saving, references, and import/export. Initialization and cleanup are session-sensitive, so code running inside Maya must not blindly repeat standalone initialization. Preserve native references, plugin dependencies, and save/reopen evidence; a batch process is not proof of target-engine compatibility. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2022/CHS/Maya-SDK/Maya-Python-API/PythonOutsideMayaSession.html",children:"Primary source"}),". ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2026/ENU/Maya-Tech-Docs/CommandsPython/file.html",children:"Maya 2026 file command"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsx(n.h3,{id:"substance-3d-painter--remote-control",children:"Substance 3D Painter · Remote Control"}),`
`,e.jsxs(n.p,{children:["Connects an external process to Painter scripting through its remote-control interface. Useful for driving an already running authoring application from a pipeline tool. The remote interface is distinct from headless texture baking and does not by itself establish a complete material-export contract. Qualify application version, project state, export preset, destination files, and downstream texture/color interpretation. ",e.jsx(n.a,{href:"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-dev/painter-python/tutorials/remote-control",children:"Primary source"}),"."]}),`
